\n- Integral III is an improper integral over an *infinite* domain since its lower limit is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-141209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1854f54b1c68a3a529c4fd3761b996338d92dbb779e14197d2a7654fd13665f"} {"question" "q-141209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-141209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-141209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-142390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to \n${\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-142390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is an improper integral of the second kind because the function under the integral is unbounded as we approach the *upper* integration limit from any point that lies in the interval $x\\in (-1,5):$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {5}^{-}\n$$\n\nWe can attempt to evaluate this integral by integrating $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [-1,b]$ and taking the limit as $b\\to {5}^{-}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{b\\to {5}^{-}}({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-142390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1854f54b1c68a3a529c4fd3761b996338d92dbb779e14197d2a7654fd13665f"} {"question" "q-142390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043930/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ad08f125d93e43bcceb3b87737a6603530712d196f8cf258e91333eaf8fe7e"} {"question" "q-142390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{b\\to (-1)^{-}}({\\int }_{b}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x)"] ["math" "{lim}_{b\\to +\\infty }({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x)"] ["math" "{lim}_